      en: "Lolei is a late 9th-century Hindu temple in the Roluos area of Siem Reap, Cambodia. Built in 893 AD under King Yasovarman I, the founder of Angkor, it originally consisted of four brick towers on an artificial island in a large baray (reservoir). Lolei was dedicated to the god Shiva and served as a royal monument. Today, the baray is dry, but the towers are partially preserved. The temple is known for its inscriptions, which provide historical details.",
